    Site "1" *-- "0..*" SitePageField : site_id
    Site "1" *-- "0..*" GpxTrack : site_id
    SitePageField "0..*" --> "0..1" Person : provided_by_steward_id
    SitePageField "0..*" --> "0..1" FormResponse : source_response_id
    Person "1" .. "0..*" ProfileHiddenQuestion : user_id = auth_user_id
    ProfileHiddenQuestion "0..*" --> "1" Question : question_id
    Person "1" .. "0..*" GpxTrack : user_id = auth_user_id
    Person "1" .. "0..*" FormResponse : user_id = auth_user_id
    ActivityStats ..> FormResponse : counts
    SirSummary ..> Answer : counts
    PdfJob ..> FormResponse : exports
    ExportJob ..> Attachment : zips files
    ExportJob ..> HomepageImageUpload : zips files
    ExportJob ..> GpxTrack : zips files
    ExportJob ..> PdfJob : zips completed PDFs
    Site "1" --> "0..*" ActivityPointValue : site_id
    Person "1" .. "0..*" ActivityPointEntry : user_id = auth_user_id
    Site "1" --> "0..*" ActivityPointEntry : site_id
    Site "1" --> "0..1" SiteSafety : site_id
    Site "1" --> "0..1" SitePriority : site_id
    PdfJob ..> PdfOptions : request_payload
    INatObservation ..> Site : found in the boundary

    note for Site "US 2.0.4: deleting a Site deletes its SIRs, answers, attachments,<br>homepage images, GPX tracks, Site fields, point records, safety and priority rows.<br>Today the database also deletes its site_stewards row (on delete cascade).<br>Related S3 files are deleted; protected_areas rows and Person records are kept."
    note for SitePageField "US 2.0.5: provided_by_steward_id records the steward who supplied the value.<br>source_response_id optionally records the SIR from which it came."
    note for Attachment "US 4.0.6: the identifier column can already be null. The story changes the app validation.<br>US 7.0.8: an Attachment with response_id is owned by that SIR and is deleted with it."
    note for ActivityPointEntry "Person.activity_points (the total) exists. This per-event table is still proposed (1.0.5)."
    note for ProfileHiddenQuestion "user_id, GpxTrack.user_id and ActivityPointEntry.user_id are auth.users ids.<br>Person.auth_user_id links them to a Person. There is no FK between them."
    note for ProtectedArea "US 6.0.1: the KML import (webapp/utils/kml-import-actions.ts) upserts rows on (folder, fid).<br>Since migration 20261006010000 there is no link to sites_pa.<br>Open question (6.0.1, 2.0.2): how a Site is matched to a protected area."
